def rd(f): return open(f,encoding="utf-8").read().rstrip()
ov=json.load(open("ov_quotes_verified.json")); sc=json.load(open("sample40_coding.json")); s40=json.load(open("sample40.json"))
used=[x for x in ov if x["quote"] in open("overview.md").read()]
M=[]
A=M.append
A("# Scope memo (operator copy), run s5, 2026-10-30\n")
A("Question: How has corruption, or allegations of corruption, affected U.S. foreign policy decisions or the conduct of diplomacy?\n")
A("All files are in the run directory (/Users/jbotts/frus-analysis/c3s/runs/s5). Commands are in `queries.log`; scripts are named beside each number. Item labels (N1, N2 ... A1 ... Q1 ... V1 ...) are the anchors the TRACE TABLE at the end points to.\n")
A("## 0. Coverage (reported first, as required)\n")
A("**N1 coverage.** `SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT volume_id), COUNT(*), SUM(is_front_matter), SUM(is_editorial_note) FROM document_cache;` returned `553|321749|1103|8481` (first tool call of the run). The read-only proof, `BEGIN; CREATE TABLE zz(x); ROLLBACK;` under `sqlite3 -readonly`, failed with \"attempt to write a readonly database\" (second call). Every count below is conditional on this index: 553 volumes, 321,749 documents, of which 312,169 are neither front matter nor editorial note (`SELECT COUNT(*) FROM document_cache c WHERE c.is_front_matter=0 AND c.is_editorial_note=0;`). The two second-edition volumes frus1951-54IranEd2 and frus1969-76ve15p2Ed2 hold 740 of those (`... AND volume_id IN ('frus1951-54IranEd2','frus1969-76ve15p2Ed2')`), leaving **311,429** documents (N2) in 551 volumes when the second editions are suppressed (their first editions are present). The surface counted is this index with apparatus excluded; the 740 is the size of the two second-edition volumes, not a measured overlap with their first editions (I did not re-derive the overlap).\n")
A("**Thinness flags.** (i) The index holds all 553 series volumes but is dated by `document_dates`; before 1860 it holds 143 dated non-apparatus documents for the 1840s, 158 for the 1850s and under 120 in each earlier decade (`ctrl_results.txt`, COVERAGE block). (ii) The 1990s hold 177 documents, all in frus1989-92v31. (iii) Search results in a decade with a handful of documents are not rates.\n")
A("## 1. Scope chosen, and how it was found\n")
A("**Inclusion rule (used meanwhile for the unresolved definitional choices in the overview):** a document is in the argument when it uses corruption, bribery, graft, embezzlement, kickback or illicit/questionable-payment vocabulary AND, in its own words, ties it to an American choice or to American conduct: aid, a loan, supervision, a démarche, jurisdiction, a treaty, a reporting requirement. Corruption or an allegation of it by or against a foreign government, or by Americans, all count. The wide set (vocabulary only) is the 3,058 hit documents (N3); the argument set is the 38 documents in the collection, drawn from 27 volumes (A1 lists them).\n")
A("**Steps.** (1) Vocabulary scan: a per-term count over the full-text index with controls (q3.py, output below, N6). (2) Decade and volume distribution of the union family (q4b.py, N4), to see where the vocabulary lives. (3) Reading the editors' own headings was not productive here: chapter headings rarely name corruption; candidate documents came instead from proximity searches (s.py) pairing the stem with aid, loan, supervision, Congress, extraterritoriality, and with named clients (see section 3). (4) Candidate documents were dumped whole to `docs/` (dump.py) and read in windows around each hit (kw.py). (5) A forty-document literal-share sample (sample.py, N5). (6) Archival resolution from the document source lines and the bundled JSON (section 5). (7) Vector operations (section 7).\n")
A("## 2. Measurements\n")
A("### N3 The hit family\n")
A("Expression (FTS5 on `frus_documents`, column `body_text`; stems because the index is porter-stemmed): `body_text:(corrupt OR brib* OR graft OR embezzl OR kickback OR \"questionable payments\" OR \"illicit payments\")`, joined to `document_cache` on `rowid`, with `c.is_front_matter=0 AND c.is_editorial_note=0`; second editions suppressed with `AND c.volume_id NOT IN ('frus1951-54IranEd2','frus1969-76ve15p2Ed2')`. Result: **3,058 documents in 447 volumes** (3,096 in 449 before suppression). The single stem `body_text:corrupt` alone: **2,175 documents in 399 volumes** (2,200 in 401 before). Script: q4b.py (output `q4b_results.txt`, counting surface: this index's body_text, which includes editors' footnotes, so a density blends document and editor language).\n")
A("Caution on the phrase operators: `\"questionable payments\"` and `\"illicit payments\"` are phrase matches over stems. The index's `\"questionable payments\"` query returns documents such as frus1947v08/d338 (\"question payment\") that have nothing to do with bribery; the literal TEI count for the true phrase is 1 occurrence in 1 volume (N8). The family is therefore dominated by the first five stems; the phrase terms contribute almost nothing and are not relied on.\n")
A("### N4 Decade shape (periodised on `document_dates.date_iso`, i.e. the document's own date, not the volume's series year)\n")
A("```\n"+rd("q4b_results.txt")+"\n```\n")
A("Reading: the shape is per 1,000 dated non-apparatus documents of the decade (denominator in each row, Ed2 volumes suppressed), with the top volume's share of the numerator. The 1840s and 1850s rows each rest on a single document and are not rates. The 1890s are 37% one volume (frus1894app2, the Hawaii papers), so the 1890s rate is mostly Hawaii; every later decade's top volume holds 5% to 10%. The shape: roughly 10 to 18 per 1,000 in the 1860s to 1900s, 3 to 6 in 1910 to 1949 (2.94 in the 1930s, one in 340), then 13, 20, 20 and 18 in the 1950s to 1980s.\n")
A("SQL behind each row (q4b.py): numerator `SELECT ... FROM frus_documents f JOIN document_cache c ON c.rowid=f.rowid LEFT JOIN document_dates d ON d.volume_id=c.volume_id AND d.document_id=c.document_id WHERE frus_documents MATCH <expr> AND c.is_front_matter=0 AND c.is_editorial_note=0 AND c.volume_id NOT IN (<Ed2>)`, grouped on `substr(d.date_iso,1,3)||'0s'`; denominator `SELECT substr(d.date_iso,1,3)||'0s', COUNT(*) FROM document_cache c JOIN document_dates d ON d.volume_id=c.volume_id AND d.document_id=c.document_id WHERE c.is_front_matter=0 AND c.is_editorial_note=0 AND c.volume_id NOT IN (<Ed2>) AND d.date_iso IS NOT NULL GROUP BY 1`. Three hit documents and two `corrupt` documents are undated and fall out of the table.\n")
A("### N5 Literal share and referent test on the family (house rule: a phrase count owes its literal share)\n")
A("Sample: 40 documents evenly spaced (`idx = int(i*len(hits)/40)`) from the (volume_id, document_id)-sorted list of the 3,058 hits (`core_hits.json` minus the Ed2 volumes; sample.py). The text tested is header + dateline + source_note + body_text, whitespace-collapsed. Regexes, case-insensitive for TOLERANT and case-sensitive for STRICT (stated: Python `re`, so STRICT is case-sensitive; SQL's LIKE was not used anywhere in this family):\n")
A("- STRICT (single spaces, headline forms only): `\\b(corruption|corrupt|bribery|bribe|bribes|graft|embezzlement|kickbacks?|questionable payments|illicit payments)\\b` -> **35 of 40**. The five misses (frus1944v06/d481, frus1946v08/d320, frus1951v05/d389, frus1964-68v31/d259, frus1969-76v42/d26) are all inflections (bribed, bribing, corrupting, corrupted).\n- TOLERANT (any inflection; any run of space, hyphen, comma, parenthesis or full stop between the phrase words): `(corrupt\\w*|brib\\w*|graft\\w*|embezzl\\w*|kickback\\w*|(?:questionable|illicit)[\\s\\-,().]+payments?)` -> **40 of 40**.\n- A 1.000 tolerant share tests the stemmer, not the referent. REFERENT test (hand coding of each sample window, judgement not SQL; `sample40_coding.json`): the sense of the question (corruption, bribery or graft in government or commerce, or an allegation of it) in **33 of 40**. The seven that are not: frus1882/d8 (corruption of the young, a sermon), frus1894app2/d506 (constitutional bar on bribe-takers), frus1904/d578 (embezzlement extradition), frus1952-54v08/d27 (aid as a 'bribe' to Poland, propaganda), frus1964-68v24/d653 (corruption of a legal system), frus1964-68v31/d259 (upper classes 'corrupting' the Radicals), frus1969-76v42/d26 (a joke, 'Haig has been corrupted by Lord'). The family is usable (tolerant 1.000 and referent 0.825, above the 0.80 floor), with the margin thin.\n- DECISION-LINK test (coded the same way): the window ties the vocabulary to an American decision or to American conduct in **8 of 40** (frus1862/d176, frus1952-54v13p1/d60, frus1955-57v06/d328, frus1955-57v22/d14, frus1958-60v05mSupp/dr_d1, frus1958-60v15/d411, frus1964-68v02/d265, frus1977-80v02/d190). This is a judgement by one coder reading a 260-character window, not the whole document; n=40 gives a wide interval.\n")
A("Sample table (n, pair, strict, tolerant, KWIC window):\n")
A("```\n"+"\n".join(f"{r['n']:2d} {r['pair']:30s} S={'Y' if r['strict'] else 'n'} T={'Y' if r['tolerant'] else 'n'} referent={'Y' if r['referent_ok'] else 'n'} decision={'Y' if r['decision_or_conduct_link'] else 'n'} | {s40[r['n']-1]['kwic'][:200]}" for r in sc)+"\n```\n")
A("### N6 Controls (positive and negative, same pass)\n")
A("From q3.py (apparatus excluded, Ed2 not suppressed in this table; `SELECT COUNT(*), COUNT(DISTINCT c.volume_id) FROM frus_documents f JOIN document_cache c ON c.rowid=f.rowid WHERE frus_documents MATCH ? AND c.is_front_matter=0 AND c.is_editorial_note=0`):\n```\nbody_text:\"Department of State\"   docs= 94049 vols=552   (POSITIVE control, expected nonzero everywhere)\nbody_text:\"ZZZ_IMPOSSIBLE_ZZZ\"   docs=     0 vols=0     (NEGATIVE control)\nbody_text:corrupt               docs=  2200 vols=401\nbody_text:bribe                 docs=   423 vols=224\nbody_text:bribery               docs=   303 vols=164\nbody_text:graft                 docs=   367 vols=163\nbody_text:embezzl               docs=   169 vols=84\nbody_text:kickback              docs=    18 vols=17\n```\nThe positive control fails in one volume, frus1919Parisv05 (`SELECT volume_id FROM document_cache GROUP BY volume_id EXCEPT SELECT DISTINCT c.volume_id FROM frus_documents f JOIN document_cache c ON c.rowid=f.rowid WHERE frus_documents MATCH 'body_text:\"Department of State\"'`), a Paris Peace Conference volume whose text does not use the phrase; this does not affect the corruption scan (the volume has the family zero times by the TEI scan, N8). The negative control also returned 0 in the TEI scan (551 volumes) and 0 in the false-friend pass (`body_text:zzzimpossiblezzz`). Note the string ZZZ_IMPOSSIBLE_ZZZ tokenises to three tokens in the index; it is a phrase there.\n")
A("### N7 False-friend test (a term the question supplied)\n")
A("```\n"+rd("ctrl_results.txt").split("volumes with zero")[0].strip()+"\n```\n")
A("Reading: 'corrupt' is 22.9 per 1,000 documents in the 27 volumes the argument rests on (scope S, A1) against 6.0 per 1,000 in the other 524. The control phrase 'Department of State' holds the baseline (302.0 against 301.2 per 1,000) and 'Ambassador' drifts mildly (408.3 against 352.7). So the term is not measuring the corpus; it is concentrated in the on-topic volumes. Caveat that matters: S was chosen from documents that contain the term, so some of the 3.8-fold concentration is by construction. The fair reading is only that the term is far from a baseline word. 'Ambassador' moving 16% shows that on-topic volumes also run more diplomatic (cables) than the rest.\n")
A("### N8 Spelling variants (TEI, tag-stripped counting surface), and the index's blind spots\n")
A("[TEI] surface: `tei_scan.py` read the 551 first-edition volume files, stripped tags, collapsed whitespace, and counted case-insensitive word-bounded regexes (front matter and footnotes NOT separated from document text; occurrences, not documents). Results (`tei_scan_summary.txt`):\n```\n"+rd("tei_scan_summary.txt")+"\n```\n")
A("What this shows: (a) the spelled-out family splits as corruption 2,384, corrupt 964, corrupted 95, corrupting 51, corruptly 13; bribery 429, bribe/bribes 401, bribed/bribing 139; graft 389; embezzle* 381. (b) Acronyms do not dominate here: FCPA 11 occurrences in one volume against 9 for the spelled-out act in two volumes. (c) The index cannot see some variants: `peculat` returns 0 in the index (stemmed `pecul*` also matches 'peculiar', 3,140 documents) while the TEI holds 'peculation' 24 times in 19 volumes; `defalc*` finds 16 and `malvers*` 36 documents, and the TEI holds 'defalcation' 23 and 'malversation' 32 times. The earlier per-era table in `ctrl_results.txt` (peculat/defalcat*/malversat* = 0) is a stem artefact and is retracted here; 'squeeze' (649 occurrences) is mostly the Chinese-trade and Levantine 'squeeze' and was not separated, so it is outside the family.\n")
A("### N9 What the index cannot reach (absences, with the controls that make them findings)\n")
A("- After 1989: the 1990s hold 177 non-apparatus dated documents, all in one volume (frus1989-92v31); the family has zero hits there (no 1990s row in N4), and the positive control 'Department of State' finds 130 documents dated 1990 or later (`SELECT COUNT(*) FROM frus_documents f JOIN document_cache c ON c.rowid=f.rowid JOIN document_dates d ON d.volume_id=c.volume_id AND d.document_id=c.document_id WHERE frus_documents MATCH 'body_text:\"Department of State\"' AND d.date_iso>='1990' AND c.is_front_matter=0 AND c.is_editorial_note=0` -> 130). The absence is the index's limit.\n- Before 1860: see N1's thinness flag; not a finding about the century.\n- Period and counterpart vocabulary (N10 in `ctrl_results.txt`, the eras table): extortion (5.6 per 1,000 before 1900 against 1.0 and 1.4 later), malfeasance (0.6, 0.1, 0.3), 'jobbery' (0.3 before 1900) show that the nineteenth century used other words; so the family under-counts the earlier decades relative to later ones. The counterpart vocabulary of merchants or chambers was not scanned; I flag that as undone.\n")
A("## 3. Candidate-finding searches (all with `s.py`, FTS5 MATCH on body_text, bm25 ascending, apparatus excluded)\n")
A("```\n"+"\n".join([
"body_text:corrupt AND body_text:aid                                   (914 docs)",
"body_text:NEAR(corrupt aid, 10), date 1944-01-01..1950-12-31           (5)",
"body_text:corrupt AND body_text:(China OR Chinese OR Kuomintang), 1947-06-01..1949-12-31   (120)",
"body_text:corrupt AND body_text:(Chiang OR Generalissimo), 1943..1946  (70)",
"body_text:corrupt AND (Chiang OR Generalissimo OR Nationalist*) AND (aid OR assistance) AND (withdraw* OR terminate* OR cease OR \"further aid\" OR \"white paper\"), 1949..1950   (21)",
"body_text:NEAR(corrupt Diem, 40) OR NEAR(corrupt Vietnam, 30), 1954..1963  (57)",
"body_text:corrupt AND (Marcos OR Philippine*), 1983..1990                  (8)",
"body_text:(\"questionable payments\" OR \"illicit payments\" OR \"foreign corrupt practices\" OR \"corrupt practices act\")   (30)",
"body_text:(brib* OR corrupt) AND (Minister OR Legation OR Department), 1860..1899   (343)",
"body_text:corrupt AND (loan OR receivership OR customs OR financial) AND (control OR supervision OR reform), 1900..1925   (92)",
"body_text:corrupt AND (extraterritorial* OR \"consular court*\" OR capitulations), 1860..1935   (30)",
"body_text:NEAR(corrupt Congress, 25) AND (aid OR assistance), 1950..1980  (9)",
"body_text:(corrupt AND (suspend* OR terminat* OR cutoff OR \"cut off\" OR halt*) AND (aid OR assistance OR loan*)), 1953..1980   (145)"])+"\n```\n")
A("Hits were ranked by bm25 (negative; ascending) and only the top 8 to 16 of each were looked at; the other ~1,500 hits of these queries were not read. This is why the argument set is a reading sample and not a census. Phrase counts above are search-set sizes, not published phrase counts; none is relied on as a count of a phrase.\n")
A("## 4. What I did not do\n")
A("The counterpart-vocabulary scan for pre-1900 corruption (merchants, chambers, the foreign ministry's own words) was not run beyond the TEI variant table. No density was published for 'document text' as distinct from footnotes (the index cannot separate them): every density in this memo blends the two.\n")
A("## 5. Archival scope (channels never summed)\n")
A("### A1 Came-from channel, the 38 collection documents (`document_sources`, one row per document)\n")
A("```\n"+rd("arch_collection_results.txt")+"\n```\n")
A("Overview counts: 37 of 38 carry a source line (`frus1893/d628` has no `document_sources` row); the 1961-63v01/d298 and 1964-68v05/d258 rows exist in the source lines but their repository is not stored (named_series 'Department of State, Johnson Files'; unrecognized 'Center for Military History, Dep CORDS / MACV Files, GVN Corruption 1967'). RG 59 Central Files = decimal 20 + subject_numeric 3 = **23 of 37**; lot files 3 (59 D 95 once; 89D149 twice); presidential libraries 7 (Carter 5, Eisenhower 1, Reagan 1); Library of Congress 2; Center for Military History 1; State Johnson Files 1. 23+3+7+2+1+1 = 37.\n")
A("### A2 Pointed-at channel, the 3,058 hit documents (`external_citations`, many rows per document)\n")
