A("Caveats stated before ranking: `external_citations` has no row before 1910-12-06 (earliest document date among all rows), stores the citation fragment and not the sentence, and holds only lot, library and decimal anchors. 'Came-from' over the same 3,058 documents (first block) is a different count of different things (508 of them have no source row at all). They are not added.\n")
A("### A3 Bundled-JSON resolution (script archival.py; arch3_results.txt)\n")
A("Whole-volume rankings over scope S (27 volumes of the collection; `archival_results.txt`), labelled: they are topic-undifferentiated counts for the whole volumes, not for the corruption documents. Came-from (collection-usage-index.json, generated 2026-10-20) ranks Central Files (1,133), Carter National Security Affairs (280), Johnson National Security File (278); pointed-at (external-citation-index.json, schemaVersion 2) ranks Carter National Security Affairs (293), Johnson NSF (162), Kennedy NSF (84).\n")
A("```\n"+rd("archival_results.txt")+"\n\n"+rd("arch3_results.txt")+"\n```\n")
A("Resolution notes. (1) Lot 59 D 95 appears in `curated-lot-resolutions.json` as kind `possible`, seriesRef conferenceFiles, NAID 602875 'Conference Files', RG-59, entry A1 3051B, 1949-1972, 'matched by collection name, not by control number'; `series-facts-index.json` gives creator Department of State. Office of the Secretary. Executive Secretariat, 238 linear feet, inclusive 1949-1972, access Unrestricted. NARA's creator attribution measured 56% precision on one route; the creator was checked only against the lot's description in `collection-authority.json` (Executive Secretariat) and is consistent. The match is probable, not confirmed. (2) Lot 89D149 is in `collection-authority.json` (S/P memoranda and correspondence from the Director of the Policy Planning Staff, RG 59, 12 volumes) but in none of `central-files-index.json`'s `lotFiles`, `curated-lot-resolutions.json` or `lot-claimants-index.json`: no NAID. (3) Lots 66D95 and 63D351 both resolve in `central-files-index.json` (matchType control) to NAID 2839192, 'Records Relating to National Security Council Policy Papers', RG 59, entry A1 1586E; `series-facts-index.json`: Executive Secretariat, 26 linear feet 3 inches, 1947-1979, access Restricted - Partly, FOIA (b)(1). (4) Presidential-library mapping, `presidential-library-catalog.json` (generated 2026-08-06, by title search): Johnson 'National Security Files' NAID 567979 (LBJ-NSF); Nixon 'National Security Files (Nixon Administration)' NAID 572235 (RN-NSF); Kennedy 'National Security Files' NAID 1164 (JFK-4); Eisenhower 'Ann C. Whitman Papers' NAID 643447 is the nearest title to the 'Whitman File' (unverified); no Carter 'National Security Affairs' (Brzezinski Material) or Reagan 'Rosenberg Files' record by title (Carter 'Brzezinski Collection' NAID 1104 is a different collection). Access for library holdings is not in the bundle. (5) The Central Files (decimal, RG 59) are not resolved to a NAID by `central-files-index.json` (its `numericalFile` is the Numerical File M862, an earlier series). `decimal-class-labels.json` was not used: its glosses are year-gated and I did not need a gloss. (6) Offline reach before 1940 is 11 of 695 bundled series.\n")
