A("## 7. VECTORS\n")
A("Files touched: `semantic-vectors-index.json`, `semantic-vectors-binary.bin`, `semantic-map.bin`, `semantic-map-index.json` (bundle, build 1.0 (1776)), and the Tier-2 shards under /Users/jbotts/frus-analysis/c3/SemanticVectors/ for every volume holding a candidate in the Hamming-800 pools (about 150 shards). Scripts: vecsetup.py, v0.py (digests), v1.py (baselines), v2.py (neighbours and funnel), v3.py (centroids, map, near-duplicates). Outputs: vec_v0.txt, vec_v1.txt, vec_v2.txt, vec_v3.txt.\n")
A("**V0 Digest comparison (all artifacts touched).** index `89481b1869da1880c599a6923df9a90bef19fc402c3db5a370ead2809b7e6101`; binary header, map header and the shard folder's `.generation` file carry the same 32 bytes; every shard read in v2.py was asserted equal to the index digest at read time. No mismatch; one generation throughout. Index `generated` 2026-10-15, `harvestGenerated` 2026-10-15T06:55:14, measuredRecallAt10 0.9021 (funnel Hamming-800 over 512 sign bits -> int8-512). Id round trip: 553 of 553 volumes decode to their stated n; rows covered 314,616 of 314,616. Identity throughout comes from the index segments (vecsetup.py `decode_segments`), never from an ordinal.\n")
A("**V1 Baselines at this digest.** Random pairs (Random(1877), 20,000): mean 167.1, sd 14.8, 1st percentile 132, minimum 95 of 512. k-th-neighbour distribution over a 200-document sample (Random(1877)): 1st neighbour median 82 (quartiles 71, 92); 10th median 102 (95, 108); 25th median 108 (101.25, 114). A neighbour is read against the k-th-neighbour distribution; a set's cohesion against random pairs. (vec_v1.txt)\n")
A("**V2 Nearest neighbours of a document (operation 1), with the funnel rerank (operation 6 of the appendix).** Anchors: frus1964-68v05/d258 (Calhoun, 'Coping with Corruption'), frus1922v01/d841 (Crowder's graft memorandum), frus1969-76ve09p2/d155 (Saudi agents' fees briefing). Each: exact Hamming over all 314,616 sign rows (numpy `bitwise_count`), top 10; then the Hamming-800 pool reranked by int8 cosine from the Tier-2 shards, top 10, with the calibrated figure `(cos-0.40)/0.60` (document-to-document offset 0.40 from `retrieval.scoreCalibration`; the raw cosine is labelled raw). Full lists: `vec_v2.txt`. Summary: the Calhoun memo's nearest neighbours are at Hamming 97 to 101, which is at the 10th-neighbour median (102) and nowhere near the 1st (82); they are Vietnam documents of 1959 to 1970 and half contain no corruption vocabulary (frus1958-60v01/d55, frus1964-68v04/d21, d222, frus1961-63v04/d347, frus1961-63v02/d300, d322). The Crowder graft memorandum's nearest is its sibling lottery memorandum at 73 and the next at 92; the rest sit at 99 to 103, i.e. the other Crowder despatches. The Saudi briefing's nearest are Saudi-policy documents at 69 to 81. Funnel calibrated figures run 0.80 to 0.89. All of these are suggestions: they show the vectors cluster by country and period, not by the theme of corruption. I read the non-vocabulary neighbours listed above for corruption language (kw.py with a wider pattern: venal, dishonest, squeeze, payoff, racket, profiteer, honest, scandal, improper, extort, theft, steal, pilfer, black market, irregularity) and found none in frus1964-68v04/d21, d222, frus1961-63v04/d347, frus1958-60v01/d55, frus1977-80v18/d151, frus1969-76ve09p2/d118. Baseline for the distances: V1.\n")
A("**V3 Semantic join into the database.** The V2 neighbours were joined to `document_cache` (header, is_front_matter, is_editorial_note) and `document_dates` and flagged against the corruption-vocabulary hit list (`corevocab` column in vec_v2.txt): all 30 Hamming neighbours and all 30 funnel rows are in `document_cache` (all 553 volumes are present, so no neighbour is absent from the local index), and none is front matter or an editorial note. Of the 30 Hamming neighbours, 18 are not in the vocabulary hit list (5, 6 and 7 for the three anchors).\n")
A("**V4 Centroid similarity (operation 3).** Volume centroids (the 553 volumes in index order, dequantised code x scale, raw cosine, float64; numpy printed divide/overflow warnings from its matmul that I traced to the library, not the data: all 553 centroid scales finite and norms 0.997 to 1.002). Nearest volumes: frus1964-68v05 -> v04 (0.991), v06 (0.988), v03, v02, v01; frus1922v01 -> 1922v02, 1921v01 (0.988), 1923v01; frus1977-80v03 -> 1969-76v31 (0.976), 1981-88v38 (0.971), 1969-76v03; frus1947v07 -> 1948v08 (0.985), 1948v07, 1946v10. Baseline: random volume pairs (5,000, Random(1877)) mean 0.904, sd 0.031, max 0.992. These are centroid-to-centroid raw cosines, not calibrated (the calibration offsets apply to document-to-query or document-to-document scores). They find neighbouring annuals, not a corruption theme.\n")
A("**V5 The map (operation 4).** Placement of the 38 collection documents in semantic-map.bin (layout of 2026-10-15; 140 clusters): 9 of 38 unclustered (0.237); the baseline is the unclustered share among all documents of the same 27 volumes, 4,552 of 18,886 (0.241), against 88,059 of 314,616 (0.280) corpus-wide, so the collection is not unusual on that measure. Clusters hit (terms from `semantic-map-index.json`): 29 (lao, vietnamese, vietnam, thieu; 7 documents), 3 (nanking, shanghai, chinese, tientsin; 5), 43 (zaya, crowder, airway, guatemala; 4), 42 (castro, somoza, cuban, cuba; 3), 5 (philippine ...; 2), 37 (shah, iran ...; 2) and singles in Greece, Congo, Korea, summitry, IMF and Constantinople clusters. Clusters are geography and period, not corruption; no cluster is a corruption cluster, which is why the map was used only to check where the argument documents fall.\n")
A("**V6 Near-duplicates (operation 5).** For each of the 38 collection documents, the nearest other document in the whole corpus by Hamming. One document is a reprint: frus1950v03/d728 (Truman-Attlee, second meeting, 42,064 characters) against frus1950v07/d977 (42,091 characters, 'United States Delegation Minutes of the Second Meeting of President Truman and Prime Minister...') at Hamming 13: the same meeting printed in two volumes. It is counted once in the collection. No other document has a neighbour under 65. Within the collection the closest pairs are frus1977-80v03/d230 and d248 (72), frus1922v01/d841 and d842 (73), d836 and d842 (77), frus1977-80v03/d35 and d65 (79); the mean within-collection pair distance is 155.4 against the random 167.1 (sd 14.8), a moderate cohesion explained by shared sub-topics.\n")
A("**Which overview documents were reached through a vector operation and no full-text query.** Exactly one is in the collection: frus1922v01/d836 (Crowder's letter of 5 April 1922), found as the second Hamming and funnel neighbour of the graft memorandum (V2); its text contains none of the family's words (it is the only one of the 38 collection documents absent from `core_hits.json`, the list of the 3,096 family hits; checked in a one-line comparison of `collection.fruscollection` against that file). It is cited in the overview only as the first step of the memoranda sequence. Everything else in the overview was reached by full-text queries (section 3) or by following a document's own cross-reference. No document was added from the map or from centroids.\n")
A("**Limits of this section.** Absence of a neighbour is not evidence of absence: the funnel's recall@10 is 0.9021, so about one of ten true neighbours is missed. Similarity is a lead: nothing here supports 'related' as a historical claim without reading, and the neighbours of the three anchors were read only for corruption vocabulary, not for substantive relation. No free-text embedding was possible (no embedder in this session), so no vector search by the word 'corruption' was attempted.\n")
