A("## 10. Honest limits\n")
A("(1) The argument set is a reading sample: of 3,058 hit documents I scanned about 150 snippet lines from the top of targeted searches, retrieved 66 documents whole and read keyword windows in them; selection toward documents that state a link is built in, so the 'one in five' is the better guide to prevalence than the collection is. (2) The decision-link coding is one coder's judgement of 260-character windows. (3) Counting surfaces: the index counts (body_text, blends document and footnote language, stems) and the TEI counts (tag-stripped occurrences, apparatus not separated) are different surfaces and are never mixed in a single number. (4) The `Foreign Relations` printed titles in the overview come from `manifest.json`. (5) Dates: the periodisation uses `document_dates.date_iso` (derived from the corpus's frus:doc-dateTime-min); the one visible disagreement is frus1977-80v03/d65, whose database date is 1977-10-01 while its printed dateline reads October 5, 1977; the overview uses the printed date. (6) q1.sql in the run directory had a parse error on its second statement after the first (a `.mode` dot-command ordering); its first statement produced the decade table, since superseded by q4b.\n")
